  "report_period": "Week 50 (5th Dec to 12th Dec 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Alpha Bulkers have committed their Capesize \"Antonis Angelicoussis\" 177/2007 SWS, China (SS 11/2027, DD 02/2026) to Greek interests at USD 20,5 mill, while the one-year-older \"Pompano\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS/DD 06/2026, Scrubber fitted) of TMS Dry was committed at high USD 17 mill basis delivery May'26. The Kamsarmax \"Ursula Manx\" 82/2021 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 08/2026, Ice Class 1C) from MX Shipping was committed to clients of Blumenthal at USD 33,85 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the two- years-older \"BW Japan\" 81/2019 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 05/2029, DD 05/2027, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 32,5 mill. On the Panamax sector, the \"Sfera\" 76/2006 Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 8,75 mill. For comparison, the \"Yasa Team\" 75/2006 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026) was sold a month ago at USD 9,3 mill. In addition, the two-years-older \"Star Emily\" 76/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 08/2029, DD 07/2027, Scrubber fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 8,5 mill. Island View Shipping committed their Ultramax \"IVS Windsor\" 60/2016 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026) to Greek interests at high USD 25 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"Grace Harmony\" 60/2015 Onomichi, Japan (SS 07/2030, DD 05/2028) was sold in November at high USD 24 mill. Goldenport Shipmanagement have committed their Handysize \"Ioanna D\" 34/2012 Nanjing, China (SS/DD 06/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 10,5 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the \"African Osprey\" 34/2012 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 07/2027) was sold at high USD 11 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Suezmax \"Olympic Future\" 155/2004 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 08/2029, DD 07/2027) of Onassis Group was committed at USD 30 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-younger Korean built \"Euroleader\" 159/2005 Hyundai, Korea (SS 02/2030, DD 06/2028) was sold at USD 29,3 mill. Chandris Hellas committed the MR2 \"Aegea\" 51/2008 Sls, Korea (SS 04/2028, DD 08/2026, Ice Class 1B) at USD 14,5 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older \"Nave Equinox\" 50/2007 Stx, Korea (SS 12/2027, DD 04/2026, Ice Class 1A) was committed in November at USD 14,4 mill. The MR1 \"Eco Revolution\" 39/2016 Hyundai-Vinashin, Vietnam (SS/DD 01/2026) was committed to clients of Navigazione Montanari at USD 32 mill. For reference, the same buyers acquired the sister vessel \"Eco Fleet\" 39/2015 Hyundai-Vinashin, Vietnam (SS/DD 07/2025) back in March at USD 30 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 14,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 14,000/16,000 pd range. Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. Inter-continental trips via US East Coast-US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent-Mediterranean range were fixed around usd 15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 13,100 pd for 6/9 months employment basis delivery East Coast India.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 14,000/17,000 pd range. West Coast India trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/18,000 pd. West Coast India trips into Arabian Gulf were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 19,000/21,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 190K/210K. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 18,000/20,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 180K/200K. West African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 24,000/26,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from North China into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South East Asian trips into West Coast India were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd with steels. Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. West African trips into Continent were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Continental trips into South America were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. US Gulf coastal trips were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 21,000/23,000 pd. East Coast South American coastal trips were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
